MID_EV20_014_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_014_m01_001: Haaah... Urghhh... Raaagh...
MID_EV20_014_m01_002: I can see that you are in pain, Dagda. I have\nprepared this flamma to ease your suffering.
MID_EV20_014_m01_003: Yes... Good... Give it here.
MID_EV20_014_m01_004: No one could have foreseen that the enemy had a\nway to harm you so grievously.
MID_EV20_014_m01_005: I've...seen something like that before.
MID_EV20_014_m01_006: It was long ago. Back when the progenitor god\nburned the world to ash...
MID_EV20_014_m01_007: So those damned humans still know how to\nuse them.
MID_EV20_014_m01_008: That power is too dangerous to exist. If they're not\ncareful, they'll wake the progenitor god.
MID_EV20_014_m01_009: The mistakes of the past must never be repeated.
MID_EV20_014_m01_010: Is the progenitor god truly that terrifying? Even\nfor you?
MID_EV20_014_m01_011: She is. I fear my mother more than anything else\nin this world.
MID_EV20_014_m01_012: People think they know what she is, but they've only\nseen her proxy...a mere vessel.
MID_EV20_014_m01_013: You have no idea of the terror her true form brings.
MID_EV20_014_m01_014: And how could you? No one would believe the\nenormity of it unless they saw for themselves.
MID_EV20_014_m01_015: Hmhmhm... Hahahaha!
MID_EV20_014_m01_016: Raksha! You told me I would need at least a million\nmore souls to match the progenitor god, yes?
MID_EV20_014_m01_017: Correct. That is why you must destroy the kingdom\nof Saramis.
MID_EV20_014_m01_018: I've been thinking. There was never any need\nfor that.
MID_EV20_014_m01_019: Why go to all the trouble of capturing the\nSaraminians for my sacrifice?
MID_EV20_014_m01_020: There are a million souls here. Right from the start,\nI had everything I needed in Dagsion.
MID_EV20_014_m01_021: Oh!
MID_EV20_014_m01_022: What?! Divine Emperor Dagda, you can't be serious!
MID_EV20_014_m01_023: Surely you're not going to throw everyone in\nDagsion into your cauldron?
MID_EV20_014_m01_024: As you wish. I will have the Order of Mithras make\nthe arrangements.
MID_EV20_014_m01_025: Good. The remaining soldiers and the temple staff\nare at your disposal as well. Make it happen.
MID_EV20_014_m01_026: Of course. All will be as you desire, Dagda.
MID_NR20_08_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_08_m01_001: The forces backing the imperial cause marched for\nDagsion, leaving troops behind to engage foes. They\nstopped on Alcineus Span—a bridge into the city.
MID_NR20_08_m01_002: The Alliance found themselves unnerved by the\ntactic, despite Troy's bold strike on the dragon Dagda\nand their resolute capture of Agris Stronghold.
MID_NR20_08_m01_003: Theodora halted her army's advance. She feared\nthat engaging the foe on that span would put them at\nrisk of being caught in a pincer maneuver.
MID_NR20_08_m01_004: Then they received far stranger news—that all of the\nother bridges into Dagsion had been demolished,\nand every ship in the harbor, burned.
MID_NR20_08_m01_005: That fully stopped their march in its tracks.
MID_NR20_08_m01_006: No further word came from the city. Theodora grew\nrestless, wanting some way forward.
MID_NR20_08_m01_007: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 3, Chapter 1
MID_EV20_015_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_015_m01_001: Demolishing bridges. Is there nothing they won't\nresort to?
MID_EV20_015_m01_062: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_063: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_064: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_065: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_066: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_067: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_002: Apart from its waterways, Dagsion's only link to the\noutside world was by bridge.
MID_EV20_015_m01_003: It has a vast stockpile of supplies. A siege approach\ncould take years.
MID_EV20_015_m01_004: And on Alcineus Span, the sole remaining way to\ncross, they're completely dug in.
MID_EV20_015_m01_005: We'd have to whittle away at their forces—for who\nknows how long—to send any troops that way.
MID_EV20_015_m01_006: Agreed. The choke point they enjoy would prevent us\nfrom putting our greater numbers to use.
MID_EV20_015_m01_007: It would also leave us open to a pincer attack from\nbehind. We must forestall that approach first.
MID_EV20_015_m01_008: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_009: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_010: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_011: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_012: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_013: Could we use the aqueducts that go into Dagsion?
MID_EV20_015_m01_014: I talked about it with Tialla. We think they're big\nenough for people to walk across.
MID_EV20_015_m01_015: I thought maybe we climb up and get in that way.
MID_EV20_015_m01_016: It is attractive in theory. But armored soldiers would\nfind it difficult to climb the structure.
MID_EV20_015_m01_017: The aqueducts are also said to have their own\ndefenses. So that approach is not feasible.
MID_EV20_015_m01_018: Oh... I thought I was on to something.
MID_EV20_015_m01_020: I will cut my way through the enemy guard alone.\nYou may follow in my wake.
MID_EV20_015_m01_021: It strains my patience to do nothing. My blade thirsts\nfor combat.
MID_EV20_015_m01_022: Much as I admire your...courage, that is not a plan.
MID_EV20_015_m01_023: The time will come when we need your fearsome\nstrength. Hold it in reserve until then.
MID_EV20_015_m01_024: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_025: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_026: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_027: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_028: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_029: 
MID_EV20_015_m01_019: If only we could remove the thorn of Arago's forces\nfrom our side...
MID_EV20_015_m01_030: I have a suggestion, if you'll hear it.
MID_EV20_015_m01_031: I've taken note of the soldiers Arago has dispatched\nagainst us so far.
MID_EV20_015_m01_032: Most are from the First Division Harpyia, the Second\nDivision Dolionia, and the Third Division Claudia.
MID_EV20_015_m01_033: In other words—their main forces. Usually garrisoned\naround the royal capital, Grand Aragon.
MID_EV20_015_m01_034: If they're here instead, then who's left to defend the\nseat of the kingdom's power?
MID_EV20_015_m01_035: Our enemy is so focused on Agris Stronghold, they\nwon't see if some of our troops break off to the west.
MID_EV20_015_m01_036: But there are no roads that way. Unless...
MID_EV20_015_m01_037: Yes. An old trade route called the Salt Road cuts\nacross the Chronos Desert from Garamantes Lake.
MID_EV20_015_m01_038: If we march that way, we can catch Grand Aragon\noff guard and seize it.
MID_EV20_015_m01_039: How many warriors do you envision this taking?
MID_EV20_015_m01_040: Three thousand. Enough for the task—not too many.\nA desert crossing will be treacherous.
MID_EV20_015_m01_041: I see. There is merit to this plan, but answer me\none thing first.
MID_EV20_015_m01_042: You bear ill will toward the king of Arago. Is this\ntactic you suggest driven by a personal grudge?
MID_EV20_015_m01_043: Mm. There was a time when I might have said yes.
MID_EV20_015_m01_044: No longer. What moves me more than my hatred for\nGilchris are the people I want to save.
MID_EV20_015_m01_045: Aswan—but also my friends, their families.\nThe people of the country I once called mine.
MID_EV20_015_m01_046: If you're asking whether I would throw away my\nsoldiers' lives in service of revenge, the answer is no.
MID_EV20_015_m01_047: I would not suggest this course of action unless I\nthought it would succeed.
MID_EV20_015_m01_048: Then I owe you an apology. I thought you keen to go\nto your death out of desperation, but I was mistaken.
MID_EV20_015_m01_049: If that's the plan, I'm coming along, of course.
MID_EV20_015_m01_050: I'm not letting you out of my sight.
MID_EV20_015_m01_051: Oh? Do you have your own score to settle with\nsomeone in that land?
MID_EV20_015_m01_052: It's pretty likely that the current king of Arago was\ninvolved in the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV20_015_m01_053: But even apart from that...there's someone there I'd\nlike to meet with.
MID_EV20_015_m01_054: Your relationship to Arago intrigues me. I hope to\nhear the story in full someday.
MID_EV20_015_m01_055: Oh, but I wouldn't dream of wasting a queen's time\nwith my sorry old tale.
MID_EV20_015_m01_056: Very well. I assent to this plan.
MID_EV20_015_m01_057: I will join in your assault on Grand Aragon myself.
MID_EV20_015_m01_058: It takes special equipment to cross the desert. Do you\nsoutherners know what you're in for?
MID_EV20_015_m01_059: We are hardier than you suspect. And our contacts\nwith a variety of merchants should serve us here.
MID_EV20_015_m01_060: We shall send word to friendly suppliers to procure\nwhat we need at once.
MID_EV20_015_m01_061: As soon as that is done, we depart. Make whatever\npreparations you deem fit now.
MID_EV20_101_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_101_m01_001: Is that the whole list? Got it.
MID_EV20_101_m01_002: That is all. Surely a man like you can arrange\nthis swiftly.
MID_EV20_101_m01_003: That's eight hundred fresh jamels and enough desert\ngear for three thousand soldiers.
MID_EV20_101_m01_004: I'll get what you need, but do you really think\nmarching down the Salt Road is a good idea?
MID_EV20_101_m01_005: It is. We will take that path, and with the supplies\nyou deliver to us, we will win.
MID_EV20_101_m01_006: I see what you're up to.
MID_EV20_101_m01_007: You want to take the Salt Road straight to Grand\nAragon for an offensive there.
MID_EV20_101_m01_008: Ah! Little gets by you, I see. It would be unthinkable\nfor most people.
MID_EV20_101_m01_009: Can you see to your end? We must have these things\nat once if this is to work.
MID_EV20_101_m01_010: Of course I can. There's nothing the Vandahl Trading\nCompany can't provide.
MID_EV20_101_m01_011: But it'll cost you, Majesty—those quantities don't\ncome cheap, and for a rush delivery...
MID_EV20_101_m01_012: Alas, my costs are mounting and finances are tight.\nAdd it to my bill for now.
MID_EV20_101_m01_013: Damn. Do you have any idea what a terrible\ncustomer you are?
MID_EV20_101_m01_014: At this rate, I really do need you to win, or else\nI'll be drowning in red ink.
MID_EV20_101_m01_015: And that won't be half as bad as the scolding I'll\nget from Ursula.
MID_EV20_101_m01_016: You needn't worry. We shall prevail.
MID_EV20_101_m01_017: Will you? And what makes you think I won't go\nrunning to Arago about this?
MID_EV20_101_m01_018: You won't. Integrity and an eye for opportunity are\nimportant to a merchant.
MID_EV20_101_m01_019: Or so you once said to me.
MID_EV20_101_m01_020: Heh. Well, you got me there. Score one for you.
MID_EV20_101_m01_021: I am choosing to put my trust in you. Our lives\ndepend upon it.
MID_NR20_04_m01: <SH>
MID_NR20_04_m01_001: Theodora made preparations for the covert march,\nworking with merchants she could trust to secure\nenough supplies and jamels to carry them.
MID_NR20_04_m01_002: Then with an elite force culled from their army at\nAgris Stronghold, she and her allies departed\nquietly—equipped in secret, leaving without word.
MID_NR20_04_m01_003: They traveled a winding path to reach the start of\nthe Salt Road. This old trading route began at\nGaramantes Lake and crossed Chronos Desert.
MID_NR20_04_m01_004: Their journey north through the heat was torment.
MID_NR20_04_m01_005: The hardships and suffering were extreme, but\nthey endured with few losses of life. At last, this\nelite force marched up to Grand Aragon, royal\ncapital of Arago.
MID_NR20_04_m01_006: —Saint Cichol, "History of the Dagdan War,"\nPart 3, Chapter 3
MID_EV20_017_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_017_m01_001: Report! What is happening at the front line? Why are\nthey not dead?!
MID_EV20_017_m01_002: We hear that the Alliance is hunkered down at\nAgris Stronghold, horns locked with our soldiers'.
MID_EV20_017_m01_003: The bulk of the empire's army is at Alcineus Span,\nblocking their passage to Dagsion.
MID_EV20_017_m01_004: It's a deadlock, but not to worry—they'll dry out\nbefore we do.
MID_EV20_017_m01_005: Ughhh. I'm certainly feeling the chancellor's absence.\nShe'd have a plan.
MID_EV20_017_m01_006: King Gilchris, terrible news!
MID_EV20_017_m01_007: The Saramis-Brezarant Alliance has made it to the\nGorbea Stronghold Ruins!
MID_EV20_017_m01_008: That's... They're at our doorstep! How the hell did \nthis happen?!
MID_EV20_017_m01_009: It seems they came north on the Salt Road.
MID_EV20_017_m01_010: Madness. Sending armored soldiers to traverse that\npassage?
MID_EV20_017_m01_011: Ughhh! Oh, they think they've outwitted me. Ha!\nWhat are their numbers?
MID_EV20_017_m01_012: Sir! Three thousand, give or take!
MID_EV20_017_m01_013: Then see that all divisions are called back to\nGrand Aragon. Immediately!
MID_EV20_017_m01_014: B-but sir, we have soldiers stationed all over the\ncountry, and they can barely put down the revolts.
MID_EV20_017_m01_015: Remove them, we risk turning the entire land over\nto chaos. So...
MID_EV20_017_m01_016: So send them back after, to slaughter the insurgents\nin every region!
MID_EV20_017_m01_017: But first and foremost is defending the capital. Am I\nwrong? Tell me I'm wrong!
MID_EV20_017_m01_018: Your Majesty—it's reported that the traitor Bertrand\nis among the enemy army.
MID_EV20_017_m01_019: H-heh. Come for another round, has he?
MID_EV20_017_m01_020: Where is the chancellor? Where is Stepmother?
MID_EV20_017_m01_021: Why has she abandoned me when I need her most?
MID_EV20_017_m01_022: Nothing has been heard of Chancellor Martila since\nshe vanished in Dagsion—and that was months ago.
MID_EV20_017_m01_023: Stepmother... He's back. Why have you left\nme alone?
MID_EV20_017_m01_024: He's going to take it all from me—my kingdom,\nmy queen. Everything.
MID_EV20_017_m01_025: Oh, I see. This is my test.
MID_EV20_017_m01_026: I'll kill him once and for all...and Aswan's heart will\nfinally be mine!
MID_EV20_018_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_018_m01_001: There seems to be a lot happening out in the castle.
MID_EV20_018_m01_002: Yeah, now you mention it. Strange.
MID_EV20_018_m01_003: Oh! Something was thrown through the window.\nIs that a rock?
MID_EV20_018_m01_004: It has a letter wrapped around it. Might be a message\nfrom our royalist allies.
MID_EV20_018_m01_005: I'll just give it a quick once-over, Your Highness. Hm.
MID_EV20_018_m01_006: Queen Aswan, listen! This is urgent.
MID_EV20_018_m01_007: The Saramis-Brezarant Alliance is marching on\nthe capital.
MID_EV20_018_m01_008: Striding in front of their army is... Stay calm when I\nsay this.
MID_EV20_018_m01_009: It's Bertrand. He's leading their forces.
MID_EV20_018_m01_010: He came back!
MID_EV20_018_m01_011: The royalists are planning to use the chaos and\nconfusion to set you free.
MID_EV20_018_m01_012: They're calling for supporters within Grand Aragon\nto rise to action.
MID_EV20_018_m01_013: We'd best join them, Tahonia. But before we do,\nI need a weapon.
MID_EV20_018_m01_014: Actually, Your Highness, you've already got one.
MID_EV20_018_m01_015: Oh, thank you, Tahonia! Let us charge forward.
