MID_EV20_021_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV20_021_m01_001: Queen Theodora! A pair of strange visitors has\narrived, asking to speak with Your Majesty.
MID_EV20_021_m01_051: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_052: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_053: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_054: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_055: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_056: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_002: Now? We already haven't a moment to spare.\nWho are they?
MID_EV20_021_m01_003: I'm not entirely sure. But there's something very\nunusual about them.
MID_EV20_021_m01_004: Thank goodness we finally made it here.
MID_EV20_021_m01_005: Hm? These people have the scent of strength about\nthem. Who are they?
MID_EV20_021_m01_006: Orchel told me about you, Theodora. She mentioned\nyou were kind to her.
MID_EV20_021_m01_007: Do you have some connection with that cat priest?
MID_EV20_021_m01_008: Yes. I am Credna, known by most as the Spark of the\nForge in the Dagdan Empire.
MID_EV20_021_m01_009: This is my mother, Jurah, whom they call the\nGiver of Fertility.
MID_EV20_021_m01_010: Credna and Jurah?! Is this true?
MID_EV20_021_m01_011: {SetColor=Gray}They're gods too? Just like Mom?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV20_021_m01_057: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_012: It is a pleasure to meet you at last, graceful queen\nof Saramis.
MID_EV20_021_m01_013: I, my mother, and my little sister Kalla have decided\nto support your alliance.
MID_EV20_021_m01_014: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_015: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_016: We are grateful, to be sure, but are you certain?
MID_EV20_021_m01_017: In all honesty, Father is a problem that I and my\nsiblings should have addressed.
MID_EV20_021_m01_018: But we stood by while my older brother Solel handled\nit alone. And look where that's gotten us.
MID_EV20_021_m01_019: Thinking back, there were signs for a long time that\nFather was headed down the wrong path.
MID_EV20_021_m01_020: Which resulted in countless terrible tragedies.
MID_EV20_021_m01_021: One of which claimed the life of someone dear to me.\nThough that was long, long ago.
MID_EV20_021_m01_022: What drove Dagda the Great to such madness?
MID_EV20_021_m01_023: I can think of only one cause: flamma.
MID_EV20_021_m01_024: We noticed a change in him after he started\nconstantly drinking it.
MID_EV20_021_m01_025: Especially after his cauldron was complete and he\nbegan to consume massive quantities of flamma.
MID_EV20_021_m01_026: It was clear that the flamma did not merely augment\nhis strength.
MID_EV20_021_m01_027: It was steadily eating away at his mind.
MID_EV20_021_m01_028: Flamma is extracted by melting down the human\nbody and soul.
MID_EV20_021_m01_029: Those who drink it take in the memories and residual\ncares of others, along with their power.
MID_EV20_021_m01_030: No mind could withstand the amounts of it he\nwould drink.
MID_EV20_021_m01_031: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_032: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_033: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_034: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_035: About five hundred years ago, Dagda the Great lost\nhis mind and killed all his caretakers.
MID_EV20_021_m01_036: When I tried to stop him, he nearly killed me as well.\nThat's when Solel arrived carrying the Bloodaxe.
MID_EV20_021_m01_037: After a desperate struggle, we defeated the emperor,\nthen secretly confined him in his crypt.
MID_EV20_021_m01_038: We told everyone that Dagda the Great had fallen\ninto a long slumber. Solel took up his duties.
MID_EV20_021_m01_039: So that's how it happened? Unbelievable...
MID_EV20_021_m01_040: 
MID_EV20_021_m01_041: But I worry that even Father was a puppet in\nsomeone else's scheme.
MID_EV20_021_m01_042: How so? Who could pull the strings of a god so\nmighty as he?
MID_EV20_021_m01_043: It was Magistra Raksha who told Father about\nflamma. She supplied it to him.
MID_EV20_021_m01_044: I believe she did this with some greater purpose\nin mind.
MID_EV20_021_m01_045: Such as?
MID_EV20_021_m01_046: It's only a hypothesis. I don't have the data to draw\na proper conclusion just yet.
MID_EV20_021_m01_047: If I'm right, it may be too terrible to consider.
MID_EV20_021_m01_048: So all this time, he was dancing to her tune. Is that\nwhat you're saying?
MID_EV20_021_m01_049: Queen Theodora! We've received a message from the\nmain force at Agris Stronghold!
MID_EV20_021_m01_050: It says that something is wrong in Dagsion. We've\nbeen asked to return immediately!